rite-021", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Under Naples lie the Catacombs of Saint Gaudiosus, paleo-Christian burials of the 4th–5th century AD, where an arcosolium at the entrance guards his tomb with a sixth-century mosaic."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-021 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the catacombs lie under Naples [S1]; they are paleo-Christian burials [S1]; they date to the 4th-5th century AD [S1]; an arcosolium at the entrance guards the tomb of the saint [S5]; the tomb has a sixth-century mosaic decoration [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-063 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Catacombs of Saint Gaudiosus are underground burial sites (catacombs) - the kind of place the text is about. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; The catacombs lie under (in) the city of Naples. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; The burials are paleo-Christian. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; The catacombs date to the 4th-5th century AD. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; The catacombs are named for Saint Gaudiosus, whose tomb they hold (traditionally his burial site). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; An arcosolium at the entrance guards the tomb of (Saint) Gaudiosus. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]; The tomb has a sixth-century mosaic. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catacombs_of_Saint_Gaudiosus]"}]'::jsonb),
