7-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the suburbs of today''s capital lie the remains of Panamá Viejo, founded in 1519, once a base for gold and silver bound for Spain, destroyed in 1671 by the Welsh privateer Henry Morgan."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-024 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the remains of Panamá Viejo lie in the suburbs of today''s capital [S1, S2]; it was founded in 1519 [S3]; it was a base for gold and silver sent to Spain [S6]; it was destroyed in 1671 [S1]; the destroyer was the Welsh privateer Henry Morgan [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-071 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Panamá Viejo is the remaining part (the remains) of the original Panama City, the former capital [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]; The remains lie in the suburbs of today''s capital [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]; It was founded in 1519 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]; It was once a base for gold and silver bound for Spain [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]; It was destroyed in 1671 by Henry Morgan [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]; Henry Morgan was a Welsh privateer [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panam%C3%A1_Viejo]"}]'::jsonb),
