.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; Long Low consists of two round cairns joined by a bank [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; The layout is unique in England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; The site was excavated in 1849 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; It has a limestone burial chamber [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; The chamber yielded the bones of thirteen people [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]; It also yielded three leaf-shaped flint arrowheads [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Low,_Wetton]"}]'::jsonb),
