09-27-01-write-025", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On the western bank of the Mur, Vespasian made Flavia Solva a municipium around year 70. First destroyed in 166, it rose again under Commodus and a few decades later flourished once more."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-025 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site lay on the western bank of the Mur [S2]; Vespasian made Flavia Solva a municipium [S3]; this happened around year 70 [S3]; it was first destroyed in 166 [S4]; it was rebuilt under Commodus [S5]; a few decades later it flourished again [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-075 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Flavia Solva was a Roman municipium (town) in the province of Noricum, in Styria, Austria [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; Flavia Solva lay on the western bank of the Mur river [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; Vespasian made Flavia Solva a municipium (raised the settlement to a town named after the Flavian family) [SUPPORTED: https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; The municipium was made around the year 70 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; Flavia Solva was first destroyed in 166 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; The city was rebuilt (rose again) under Commodus [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]; A few decades after the rebuilding the city flourished once more [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavia_Solva]"}]'::jsonb),
